    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the most common washdown conveyor problems?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The most common washdown conveyor problems are premature bearing failure from water and chemicals washing out grease, water intrusion into motors rated below the cleaning method, harborage points in hollow frames and lap joints, belt slip and mistracking on wet friction-driven belts, and chemical attack on 304 stainless, aluminum, plastics, or seals. Most trace back to components rated for a lighter cleaning program than the plant actually runs."
      }
